  {
   "id": "vliw",
   "steps": [
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Stage 4: VLIW, very long instruction word. Move all that checking out of the hardware and into the compiler."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "replace",
       "target": "head",
       "text": "Stage 4 of 7: VLIW"
      },
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "ssx"
      },
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "takeaway"
      },
      {
       "action": "show",
       "target": "vcode"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Take these six statements. The add, the multiply and the load do not depend on each other. g needs a and d, and the branch needs g."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "mark_lines",
       "target": "vcode",
       "from": 1,
       "to": 3
      },
      {
       "action": "goto_line",
       "target": "vcode",
       "line": 5,
       "delay": 0.5
      },
      {
       "action": "goto_line",
       "target": "vcode",
       "line": 6,
       "delay": 0.8
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Each instruction word has fixed slots, one for each functional unit: here an integer ALU, a multiplier, a memory unit and a branch unit."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "vcode"
      },
      {
       "action": "show",
       "target": "vliw"
      },
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "vliw[0]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "The compiler finds that the add, the multiply and the load are independent, and packs them into word 1."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "vliw[0]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "g needs a and d, so it must wait for word 2. The store can share that word."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "vliw[1]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "The branch needs g, so it goes alone in word 3."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "vliw[2]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Every slot the compiler cannot fill holds a NOP: 6 of the 12 slots here are wasted."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "mark",
       "target": "vliw[0][4]"
      },
      {
       "action": "mark",
       "target": "vliw[1][2]",
       "delay": 0.2
      },
      {
       "action": "mark",
       "target": "vliw[1][4]",
       "delay": 0.4
      },
      {
       "action": "mark",
       "target": "vliw[2][1]",
       "delay": 0.6
      },
      {
       "action": "mark",
       "target": "vliw[2][2]",
       "delay": 0.7
      },
      {
       "action": "mark",
       "target": "vliw[2][3]",
       "delay": 0.8
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "So the hardware is simple, because it never checks for dependences. But there is a price."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "vliw"
      },
      {
       "action": "show",
       "target": "vx"
      },
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "vx[0]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "NOPs make the code larger. And because the slots are part of the instruction set, a wider model needs the program recompiled."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "vx[1..=2]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "And the compiler cannot predict a cache miss, so when one operation waits, the whole word waits with it."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "vx[3]"
      },
      {
       "action": "write",
       "target": "takeaway"
      },
      {
       "action": "replace",
       "target": "takeaway",
       "text": "VLIW: the compiler finds the parallelism ahead of time"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
